// Cloudflare deploy config.
//
// Cloudflare Pages is now served by Workers, and `wrangler pages deploy` no
// longer works against a project created by current wrangler. This is the
// Workers form of the same thing: a Worker with no code of its own, serving a
// directory of static assets.
//
// `directory` is the dangerous line. `wrangler pages project create` scaffolds
// this file with `"directory": "."`, which publishes the entire repository: on
// 2026-09-18 that put tools/, COPY.md, README.md, LICENSE and .git/config on
// the live origin, which is the whole thing the allowlist exists to prevent.
// It must stay pointed at the built output that tools/build-dist.sh assembles.
//
// `name` matters too: it is the deployed Worker, and changing it publishes a
// second one at a different URL rather than updating this one.
//
// tools/check.py fails if either line changes, and tools/deploy.sh re-checks
// the live origin after every deploy.
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "promptdecode",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-18",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "dist",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  },
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
